      "side": 1,
      "message": "They are not quite the same, though the idea is similar. kb_input_asserted() is intended as a quick snapshot of the state of the inputs while num_keys_pressed reflects the result of a full scan.\n\nSince this is a do-while loop and the scan is executed before the condition is checked, num_keys_pressed can be used. Now that you mention it, num_keys_pressed seems like a better choice since it\u0027s just a variable and doesn\u0027t need to do everything kb_input_asserted() does.\n\nkb_input_asserted() is better suited for use immediately before we put the task to sleep.",
